title "Printers/Copiers Example"

# not modelled: "Used on the Incident Record" callout (Service / Offering / CI
#   arrows to the Business Service, an offering and the CI), domain legend,
#   note that Business Capabilities are not depicted, note that the Dynamic CI
#   Group could also be related to a Business Service Offering

SP end-user-portfolio: End User Services Portfolio
SP tech-portfolio: Technology Services Portfolio

BS print-copy: Print and Copy Services
BSO std-laser: Std Laser Printers
BSO exec-desktop: Executive Desktop Printers
BSO managed-copiers: Managed Copiers

SI print-server: Print Server
BA hp-print-mgmt: HP Print Mgmt Admin

TMS print-mgmt: Print Management Services
TMSO print-server-admin: Print Server Admin
TMS tms-tbd: TBD
TMSO printer-admin: Printer Administration
DCG printers: Printers (by location, brand, support)
CI printer: Printer Name

print-copy -> end-user-portfolio
std-laser -> print-copy
exec-desktop -> print-copy
managed-copiers -> print-copy

print-mgmt -> tech-portfolio
print-server-admin -> print-mgmt
print-server-admin -> print-server

hp-print-mgmt -> print-server
managed-copiers -> print-server
# Orange "Depends On" connector from Std Laser Printers only (the white line
# crossing it belongs to Executive Desktop Printers).
std-laser -> print-server

printer-admin -> tms-tbd
printer-admin -> printers
printers -> printer
# White "Contains" connector from Executive Desktop Printers down into the
# Dynamic CI Group (BSO -> DCG is not a standard CSDM pair; kept as shown).
exec-desktop -> printers : Contains
